7. Chinese-language variant
Use the same skeleton and the same section order.
Element	Standard text
Salutation	`尊敬的客户，`
Opening	`我们的回复如下：` / `关于贵公司询问的[主题]，我们的回复如下：`
Assumptions	`我们的回复基于以下假设：` … `如以上理解有误，请告知我们，因为税务处理可能有所不同。`
Conclusion connector	`因此，……`
Quote intro	`根据《Income Tax Act 1967》第XX条规定：` / `根据 PR X/YYYY 第X段：`
Disclaimer heading	`免责声明`
Disclaimer	`以上意见仅基于贵公司所提供的资料及所列假设，仅供一般参考。实际的[税种]处理可能因具体事实、合约条款及相关文件而有所不同，建议在作出最终决定前审阅相关文件。`
Sign-off	`谢谢。`
Rules:
Keep statute names, form names and technical terms in English (e.g. Income Tax Act 1967, EA Form, Benefit in Kind, self-billed e-Invoice, WHT).
Quote provisions in their original language (English / BM) and follow each quote with a Chinese explanation.
Use full-width punctuation (，。：；) in Chinese sentences.
---
8. Length and tone
Target length: 250–700 words for a single issue; about 300 words for each additional tax in a multi-tax answer. Over 1,000 words is a sign the answer should be split.
Lead with the answer. The first sentence of each section should state the position. Explain afterwards.
One conclusion per section. Do not repeat the conclusion in a closing summary unless the answer has four or more sections.
Follow-ups: answer only what changed. Open with `Further to your clarification on [point], …` and reuse the original section numbering where possible.
---
9. Pre-submission checklist
[ ] `Dear Valued Customer,` / `尊敬的客户，`
[ ] Scenario not restated; the assumptions list only facts that change the outcome
[ ] Numbered, subtitled sections, in the multi-tax order where more than one tax is covered
[ ] Each section: principle → quoted authority → application → "Accordingly, …"
[ ] At least one authority cited, with its operative wording quoted verbatim and the reference on the same line
[ ] Defined terms used consistently (Section 2)
[ ] Point form only for conditions / criteria / document lists
[ ] `Disclaimer` heading and the correct variant, naming every tax covered
[ ] `Thank you.` / `谢谢。` as the final line
[ ] Category set to the main tax issue; other taxes added to Tags
